# Backend security

## Input validation

- **FluentValidation** - use FluentValidation for DTO validation
- **Controller-level validation** - validate data before processing

Example:
```csharp
if (!ModelState.IsValid)
{
    foreach (var error in ModelState)
    {
        _logger.LogWarning("ModelState error for {Key}: {Errors}",
            error.Key,
            string.Join(", ", error.Value.Errors.Select(e => e.ErrorMessage)));
    }
}
```

## Data sanitization

- **Sanitize input** - sanitize all user data before use
- **XSS protection** - escape HTML/JavaScript in user input
- **SQL Injection protection** - use parameterized queries; do not use string concatenation

## Logging sensitive data

- **Do not log sensitive data** - do not log passwords, tokens, or personal data
- **Data masking** - mask sensitive data in logs (e.g. `****` instead of password)
- **Structured logging** - use parameterized messages for logging

Example:
```csharp
// ❌ Bad
_logger.LogInformation("User login: {Username}, Password: {Password}", username, password);

// ✅ Good
_logger.LogInformation("User login attempt: {Username}", username);
```

## CORS

- **CORS configuration** - configure CORS policy for allowed origins
- **Middleware order** - CORS must be configured before middleware that reads headers
- **AllowCredentials** - use `AllowCredentials()` for cookie support

Example:
```csharp
services.AddCors(o =>
{
    o.AddPolicy("ui", builder =>
    {
        builder
            .WithOrigins(configuration["Cors:AllowedOrigins"]!.Split(","))
            .AllowAnyHeader()
            .AllowAnyMethod()
            .AllowCredentials()
            .WithExposedHeaders("Set-Cookie");
    });
});

// In ConfigureApp - CORS must be before other middleware
app.UseCors("ui");
```

## HTTPS

- **HTTPS in production** - use HTTPS in production
- **HSTS** - use HTTP Strict Transport Security (HSTS) in production
- **HTTPS Redirection** - redirect HTTP to HTTPS in production

Example:
```csharp
if (!app.Environment.IsDevelopment())
{
    app.UseHsts();
    app.UseHttpsRedirection();
}
```

## Attack protection

- **Rate Limiting** - use rate limiting for DDoS protection
- **Request Size Limits** - limit request size (especially for file uploads)
- **Timeout** - set timeouts for long operations

Example size limit:
```csharp
services.Configure<FormOptions>(options =>
{
    options.MultipartBodyLengthLimit = 10485760; // 10 MB
    options.ValueLengthLimit = int.MaxValue;
});
```

## Security headers

- **Security Headers** - set security headers (X-Content-Type-Options, X-Frame-Options, etc.)
- **Custom Headers** - use middleware for custom security headers

## API protection

- **API Versioning** - use API versioning to control changes
- **Rate Limiting per User** - limit requests per user
- **IP Whitelisting** - use IP whitelisting for critical endpoints (if needed)
